      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two hundred patients with unstable angina were examined. Of those, 100 were on medication only, while another 100 had undergone aortocoronary shunting. Five-year survival rate was higher, and the quality of life was better, in the surgical patients, as compared to conservative cases."},
